---
// Clean, Flat Educational Guide matching realonlineruler.com (Images 3 & 4)
// No curved corners, no neon, authentic humanized technical prose.
---

<section id="guide" class="relative z-10 w-full bg-[var(--bg-main)] text-[var(--text-primary)] border-t border-[var(--border-color)] rounded-none shadow-[0_-20px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.5)]">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 space-y-12">
    <!-- Main Headline & Definition -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
        Free Online Protractor: Measure Actual Angles in Degrees, Radians and Slope
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        Online Protractor turns your screen into a calibrated precision angle finder. Align the origin eyelet on your vertex, set your baseline, and rotate the hairline indicator arm to measure acute, obtuse, right, or reflex angles. It runs entirely inside your browser on mobile phones, tablets, Chromebooks, and desktop monitors with zero plugins or downloads.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        Beyond measuring on-screen vectors, you can paste screenshots directly from your clipboard (<kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded font-mono text-xs">Ctrl+V</kbd>), upload reference diagrams, or stream live video through your device camera to measure physical objects in real time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Start Guide -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
        How to measure an angle in three steps
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] space-y-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-[var(--text-muted)]">01</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Position the Vertex</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            Drag the center brass pivot directly over the intersection point where your two rays or lines meet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] space-y-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-[var(--text-muted)]">02</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Align the Baseline</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            Align the base pin flat along the reference edge of your shape, worksheet, or image. Click Flip to mirror 180°.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] space-y-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-[var(--text-muted)]">03</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Rotate the Indicator</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            Drag the white indicator knob along the second line. Read live degrees, radians, and slope, or press Copy to export.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Features Breakdown -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
        Core measurement capabilities
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] space-y-1.5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Drag-to-Measure Hairline Arms</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            Smooth continuous angle rotation with optional 5° magnetic snap for quick locking on common architectural pitches and geometry benchmarks (30°, 45°, 60°, 90°, 120°).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] space-y-1.5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Measure Angles on Images & Blueprints</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            Drag and drop images or press <kbd class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-[var(--bg-main)] border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded font-mono text-[10px]">Ctrl+V</kbd> to paste screenshots. Pan, scale, and rotate photos directly behind the transparent protractor overlay.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] space-y-1.5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Live Camera Angle Overlay</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            Point your mobile or laptop camera at physical objects, wood miters, or sheet metal to measure angles without touching paper rulers to physical surfaces.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] space-y-1.5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">180° Semi-Circle & 360° Full Disc</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            Toggle between standard 180° dome geometry and full 360° disc mode to calculate reflex angles, azimuth compass bearings, and multi-quadrant rotations.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Practical Use Cases -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
        Common applications
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 text-xs text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)]">
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">Geometry & Mathematics Homework</strong>
          Paste screenshot captures of PDF worksheets or digital textbook problems. Use 180° mode with 5° snap to solve acute, obtuse, and complementary angle assignments.
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)]">
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">UI/UX & Graphic Design QA</strong>
          Inspect icon slants, diagonal hero section dividers, and isometric grid artwork by pasting Figma or web screenshots with snap disabled.
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)]">
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">DIY Woodworking & Construction Verification</strong>
          Take a photo of roof pitches, stair stringers, or mitered trim molding. Scale and rotate the photo to verify joint angles before making table saw cuts.
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)]">
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">Classroom Projector Demonstrations</strong>
          Display the high-contrast dark theme on smartboards and classroom projectors for angle demonstrations without plastic classroom kits.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conversion & Classification Table -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
        Angle classifications and conversion reference
      </h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-none border border-[var(--border-color)]">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
          <thead class="bg-[var(--bg-card)] text-[var(--text-primary)] border-b border-[var(--border-color)]">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Angle Type</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Degree Range</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Radians</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Typical Application</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--border-color)] bg-[var(--bg-main)] text-[var(--text-secondary)] font-mono">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Acute</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">&gt; 0° and &lt; 90°</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">&lt; 1.571 rad</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans">Roof rafter pitches, scissor cuts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Right</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">Exactly 90°</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">π/2 rad (1.571)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans">Square framing, perpendicular joints</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Obtuse</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">&gt; 90° and &lt; 180°</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">1.571 to 3.142 rad</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans">Miter joints, reclining angles</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Straight</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">Exactly 180°</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">π rad (3.142)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans">Flat horizontal baseline</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Reflex</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">&gt; 180° and &lt; 360°</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5">&gt; 3.142 rad</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-sans">Navigational bearings, outer door swing</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Practical Tips for Accurate Measurement -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight">
        Tips for accurate angle measurements
      </h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-semibold">Keep browser zoom at 100%.</strong>
          Press <kbd class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded font-mono text-xs">Ctrl+0</kbd> (Windows) or <kbd class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-[var(--bg-card)] border border-[var(--border-color)] rounded font-mono text-xs">Cmd+0</kbd> (Mac) to prevent fractional coordinate rounding.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-semibold">Look straight at the display.</strong>
          Viewing through thick laptop cover glass from an angle causes optical parallax. Always align the vertex looking straight down at the screen.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-semibold">Use image editing mode.</strong>
          When measuring photos or blueprints, click <strong class="text-blue-400">Edit Image</strong> to scale and rotate the background so your lines sit flat against the protractor baseline.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
